# .clinerules — Form Review Agent (DocDesk)

Rules Cline must follow while working in this repository.

## Before Acting
- Always propose a plan and wait for approval before creating or editing files (Plan mode → confirm → Act mode).
- Confirm the exact function signature, inputs, and outputs before writing any new function.
- Never assume a field name — the project's data contract uses exactly: `name`, `dob`, `id_number`, `address`, `income`, `category`. Do not rename or add keys without flagging it first.

## Code Standards
- Every function must have type hints and a docstring.
- Every new function ships with at least one pytest test file in `tests/`, covering a normal case and an edge case.
- Prefer deterministic, rule-based logic over live AI calls inside core decision functions (extraction, verification, risk scoring, routing). AI calls are only used to generate human-readable summaries **from** already-computed structured data — never to produce the structured data itself.
- If a value can't be confidently determined, return `None`. Never guess or invent a value.
- Keep functions small and single-purpose. Split anything doing more than one clearly describable thing.

## File Ownership (do not cross-edit without being asked)
- `app/extraction.py` — field extraction (Custom Agent: Form Field Extractor)
- `app/verification.py` — missing field + cross-document checks (Custom Skill: Cross-Document Verifier)
- `app/routing.py` — risk scoring, routing, decision logging, audit history
- `app/security.py` — encryption, file handling, API key auth, PII-safe logging
- `app/duplicate_detection.py` — SHA-256 file hash duplicate detection
- `app/expiry_detection.py` — document expiry date checking
- `app/cross_check_engine.py` — stateful per-application extraction + cross-check tracking
- `app/ai_review_summary.py` — human-readable reviewer summaries (template-based by default)
- `app/pipeline_integration.py` — wires all modules into one end-to-end flow
- `main.py` — pipeline orchestration entry point / demo runner

## Testing
- Run `pytest -v` locally before any commit is suggested.
- Tests must be fully deterministic — never depend on live AI model output that could vary between runs.
- Never weaken, skip, or delete a test just to make CI pass.

## Git
- Commit messages are short and specific about *what* changed, not generic ("add X" not "update code").
- Never commit `.env`, encryption keys, or anything listed in `.gitignore`.
- One logical change per commit where practical.

## Absolute Boundaries
- Never make the final approve/reject decision on an application — the system only flags and routes; a human decides.
- Never fabricate a test result or claim code works without having actually run the tests.
- Never bypass the security layer (encryption, API key checks), even temporarily, for convenience.
